This project explores the implications of the rise of artificial intelligence (AI) technology in people’s homes, focusing on the security and privacy concerns associated with smart devices. I focused on how companies like Amazon, which offers products such as Alexa, smart bulbs, and the Ring security system, integrate AI into daily life, raising questions about data security. The project also discusses the broader impact of technology on daily activities, such as job applications and bill payments, and highlights the potential risks of sensitive data misuse as AI systems become more complex and widespread. 
